# Environment for the seedstone service. Read by systemd on start; after a
# change: systemctl restart seedstone.
#
# A password. Never an argument: a command line is readable by every
# process on the host, an environment file is not.
#SEEDSTONE_REQUIREPASS=change-me
#
# Any other flag, appended to the unit's command line. The unit already
# passes --bind 127.0.0.1:6379 and --data-dir /var/lib/seedstone; a flag
# given twice takes its last value, so a --bind here replaces the unit's.
# The service can write nowhere but /var/lib/seedstone, so a --data-dir
# elsewhere also needs the unit changed (systemctl edit seedstone).
# Every flag: docs/operations.md.
#SEEDSTONE_OPTS=--maxmemory 2gb --maxmemory-policy allkeys-lru
